
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include("./partials/head.ejs") %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/texty.css" />
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <%- include("./partials/navbar.ejs") %>
    </header>
    <main>
        <section>
            <h1>Pregame</h1>
            <p>
                Checkers/Draughts is a two player game. The first person to enter a room is assigned the color black and the other player is assigned red.
                In the case that there is just one person within the room, he becomes the room leader. The room leader always goes
                first (no matter his color).
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>
                Game Objective
            </h1>
            <p>
                The aim of the game is to capture all of your opponents pieces.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>On My turn?</h1>
            <p>
                Click on one of your pieces to see the available moves of that specific piece.
                When these appear, click on one of the possible squares to move that piece there.
                When a normal piece (pawn) gets to the last row of the opponent side of the board, it becomes
                a king (or queen). Pawns only move or capture diagonally one square away. Kings can 
                capture any diagonal distance away. All capturing is mandatory, including successive captures.
                After you make a move and there are no more moves by the same piece (captures), your turn is over
                and you must wait for your opponent to make a move.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>When does it end?</h1>
            <p>
                The game ends when you win by capturing all your opponents pieces. When this cannot be done, the game ends as a draw.
                Specific draw scenarios include there being only one piece of each side on the board, there being only kings (or queens),
                there not being any viable moves, etc. After the game ends, it can be restarted by the room leader.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
    <script>
            // definition of variables
            const showNavbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarDropdownButton");
            const navbarLine = document.getElementById("navbarLine");
            const navbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarActions");
            const mediaQuery = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 760px)");
            
            let isNavbarToggled = false;

            // toggle navbar dropdown on or off
            showNavbarActions.addEventListener("click", () => {
                isNavbarToggled = !isNavbarToggled;
                if (isNavbarToggled) {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25B2;";
                } else {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden";
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                }
            });
            function handleMediaChange(e) {
                navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                isNavbarToggled = false;
                if (e.matches) {
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden"
                    showNavbarActions.className = "";
                } else {
                    showNavbarActions.className = "hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                }
            }
            mediaQuery.addEventListener("change", e => handleMediaChange(e))
            handleMediaChange(mediaQuery);
    </script>
</body>

</html>
